comments.body:
Would it be better to change this to the following:

```js
    diagram = new Diagram(str, {config: {theme: "dark", logLevel: 1}, wrap: true});
```

(assuming that's how the new metadata argument will work, once this PR is updated with https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/pull/4750)

That way we can keep the following lines in the test, without removing them:

```js
    expect(mermaid.theme).toBe('dark');
    expect(mermaid.logLevel).toBe(1);
```

That's a good point. What does `wrap` even do?

For other diagrams, should we have something like:

```js
init: ({ wrap }) => {
  if (wrap) {
    // or maybe just print a warning?
    throw new Error("This diagram does not support %%{wrap}%%");
  }
},
```
